      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Using the trigonometric identity \\[\\sin A \\sin B = \\frac12 (\\cos (A-B) - \\cos (A+B)),\\]we see that \\begin{align*}\n\\sin 2x \\sin 3x &= \\cos 2x \\cos 3x \\\\\n\\frac12 \\cos (2x-3x) - \\frac12 \\cos (2x+3x) &= \\frac12 \\cos (2x-3x) \\\\\n\\cos (2x+3x) &= \\frac12 \\cos (2x+3x).\n\\end{align*}Thus, \\[\\cos (2x+3x) = 0.\\]Since $\\sin \\frac{n \\pi}{2}$ is 1 when \\[n \\equiv \\frac{1}{2} \\pmod{1},\\]which \\[n \\equiv \\frac{1}{2} \\equiv -\\frac{1}{2} \\pmod{1},\\]the value of $x$ is \\[\\boxed{-30} \\, \\text{degrees}.\\]. The answer is -30",
